CORE gnu-extensions
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ argument converted by the deduced specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [over.match.funcs]/8 + [temp.deduct.call]: a constructor template
contributes to a user-defined conversion the one specialization deduced
from the argument, not its earlier instantiations.  `big(T)' already
instantiated for int and for unsigned __int128 made a `unsigned long'
argument ambiguous between those two (both need an integral conversion),
so `b < limit' had no viable candidate (libstdc++ 16's __max_size_type in
the C++20 ranges iterators).
